sentences.l:
The-man in the-time of-prosperity (is) like-the-tree * and the-people around it as-long-as it-is for-the-fruit;
until, when its-load has-gone from-it, they-depart * and khaffūhā, it enduring the-heat and the-dust;
ruin to-the-sons of-this the-age, all-of-them * even (that) not one is-pure of the-ten.

sentences.i:
A man in the days of fortune is like a tree, * and men gather about it so long as it bears fruit;
but when its burden is gone from it they depart, * and leave it to bear the heat and the dust.
Shame on the sons of this age, every one of them: * not one of the ten is true.
